funcstart_shrinkwrap_el.o, funcstart_shrinkwrap_eb.o -- MIPS32 relocatable
objects whose first function returns early and sets up its frame after the
return, so a function-start pattern pair matches inside its sized symbol
(decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/src/analyzers/entry/mod.rs tests,
tests/stages/kuna-funcstart-symbolextent.xml).

What they are
  funcstart_shrinkwrap_el.o  little-endian o32, non-PIC.
  funcstart_shrinkwrap_eb.o  big-endian o32, non-PIC.
  Source: funcstart_shrinkwrap.c. buf_dup_char opens with bnez/nop/jr ra/nop
  and its addiu sp,sp,-32 prologue sits at .text+0x10, inside the symbol's
  0x74-byte extent.

Why they are vendored
  CI has no MIPS toolchain, and the test depends on gcc's exact block order.

Where they came from
  Ubuntu mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc 10.3.0 and its binutils 2.38 (host):

      mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc -O2 -mno-abicalls -fno-pic -c funcstart_shrinkwrap.c \
          -o funcstart_shrinkwrap_el.o
      mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc -EB -O2 -mno-abicalls -fno-pic -c funcstart_shrinkwrap.c \
          -o funcstart_shrinkwrap_eb.o

  sha256:
    8f6061589965d9945fc9bc6b256b0381e41f5909544011656f937c45695eb42b  funcstart_shrinkwrap_el.o
    869936712294fe61d491f1d2a928e345126ca1407c15fd7e7764647bdefa3d80  funcstart_shrinkwrap_eb.o
